abstract: Bao mian lan chu [Preventing and averting illness] is an 1867 Chinese medical
  and everyday-health booklet by Frederick Porter Smith. Bodleian Libraries, Sinica
  2044, is catalogued as published in Hankow (漢皋); its title page names Baoshan jushe
  (寶善居舍) as the block holder. It discusses housing, diet, mental and physical activity,
  cleanliness, internal and external medicine, eye conditions, women’s health and
  infant care, linking health discourse with Christian vocabulary. It supports historical
  work on medical translation, missionary publishing and everyday life in late-Qing
  China. Based on 21 Bodleian digital captures, this dataset provides an AI initial
  transcription of 36 designated physical faces, including titles, prefaces, main
  text, appendices, running margins and one originally blank framed body. TXT, JSON
  and TEI XML retain readings, uncertainties and source-image mappings. Full human
  double collation and expert review have not been performed; uncertain readings and
  clipped marginal material remain marked.
